 "answer_raw": "A dozen eggs currently cost **$2.27** on average, which is roughly **35% cheaper** than they were a year ago [1][2][5].\n\nAs of September 2026, the U.S. city average for a dozen Grade A large eggs is **$2.27** [1][2][5]. This is a significant drop from the price of **$3.49** per dozen recorded in September 2025 [1][2][5][7]. \n\nThe price has stabilized recently; after hitting a low of **$2.14** in June 2026, it rose slightly to **$2.27** in August and has remained at that level through September 2026 [2]. This current price remains well below the record high of **$6.23** set in March 2025 [2][7].",
